## 2. Free Solo use

A "Solo User" is one natural person working alone on their own project, on
their own behalf, including through a business solely owned and operated by
that person with no other working owners, employees or participating contractors.
Commercial projects are permitted. Having an unrelated job does not disqualify
someone from Solo use on their own independent project.

Solo use excludes work on a project with another person and use on behalf of an
organization with other people, including as an employee or contractor. A single
operator in a larger organization is not a Solo User. Separate accounts,
installations or memory databases do not turn a team project into Solo use.
AI agents, devices and automated processes are not additional people.

Subject to this license, a Solo User receives a worldwide, non-exclusive,
non-transferable and non-sublicensable permission, without a license fee, to
install, run, inspect and privately modify the Software for that Solo use.
Installation, backup and recovery copies are permitted. There is no limit on
that user's agents, devices, memory databases or qualifying projects.

Private hosting, storage and automated processing providers may hold or execute
necessary copies solely on the user's behalf, with access restricted to providing
those services and no independent right to use or redistribute the Software.
The user remains responsible for compliance. This does not permit providing
Dandelion functionality to other customers or team members.

